#### Variation 2: HashiCorp Consul

**Description**: Consul-based service discovery with health checking and K/V store.

**Technology Stack**:
- **Service Registry**: HashiCorp Consul
- **Discovery Client**: Consul client libraries (Go, Java, .NET, Node.js, Python)
- **Health Checking**: Consul health checks (HTTP, TCP, script-based)
- **Load Balancing**: Application-level load balancing or Consul Connect (service mesh)

**Configuration Example**:
```hcl
# Consul Server Configuration
datacenter = \"eastus\"
data_dir = \"/var/consul\"
log_level = \"INFO\"
server = true
bootstrap_expect = 3
ui = true

# Service Registration (member-service)
{
  \"service\": {
    \"name\": \"member-service\",
    \"id\": \"member-service-1\",
    \"port\": 8080,
    \"tags\": [\"v2.3.1\", \"production\", \"eastus-1\"],
    \"meta\": {
      \"version\": \"2.3.1\",
      \"zone\": \"eastus-1\"
    },
    \"checks\": [
      {
        \"http\": \"http://localhost:8080/health\",
        \"interval\": \"30s\",
        \"timeout\": \"5s\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

```csharp
// .NET Consul Client
using Consul;

public class ConsulServiceDiscovery
{
    private readonly IConsulClient _consulClient;

    public ConsulServiceDiscovery()
    {
        _consulClient = new ConsulClient(config => {
            config.Address = new Uri(\"http://consul-server:8500\");
        });
    }

    public async Task RegisterAsync()
    {
        var registration = new AgentServiceRegistration
        {
            ID = \"member-service-\" + Environment.MachineName,
            Name = \"member-service\",
            Port = 8080,
            Address = GetLocalIP(),
            Tags = new[] { \"v2.3.1\", \"production\" },
            Check = new AgentServiceCheck
            {
                HTTP = \"http://\" + GetLocalIP() + \":8080/health\",
                Interval = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30),
                Timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5),
                DeregisterCriticalServiceAfter = TimeSpan.FromMinutes(2)
            }
        };

        await _consulClient.Agent.ServiceRegister(registration);
    }

    public async Task<List<ServiceEntry>> DiscoverAsync(string serviceName)
    {
        var services = await _consulClient.Health.Service(serviceName, tag: null, passingOnly: true);
        return services.Response.ToList();
    }
}
```

**Pros**:
- ✅ Multi-datacenter support with WAN federation
- ✅ Built-in health checking (HTTP, TCP, script-based, Docker, gRPC)
- ✅ Key/value store for distributed configuration
- ✅ Consul Connect provides service mesh capabilities (mTLS, traffic management)
- ✅ Strong security features (ACLs, TLS, intentions)
- ✅ Polyglot support (official clients for Go, Java, .NET, Python, Node.js)

**Cons**:
- ❌ More complex operational setup than Eureka (requires understanding of Raft consensus)
- ❌ Learning curve for Consul-specific concepts (intentions, service segments)
- ❌ Client-side load balancing requires custom implementation (no Ribbon equivalent)

