### Configuration Best Practices

**Service Naming Conventions**:
- Use lowercase with hyphens: `member-service`, `claims-adjudication-service`
- Include domain/context: `medicaid-eligibility-service`, `provider-credentialing-service`
- Avoid version in service name: use metadata instead (`version: 2.3.1`)

**Health Check Design**:
```java
@RestController
public class HealthController {
    @Autowired
    private DataSource dataSource;

    @GetMapping(\"/actuator/health\")
    public ResponseEntity<HealthStatus> health() {
        boolean healthy = true;
        Map<String, String> details = new HashMap<>();

        // Check database connectivity
        try {
            dataSource.getConnection().close();
            details.put(\"database\", \"UP\");
        } catch (SQLException e) {
            healthy = false;
            details.put(\"database\", \"DOWN\");
        }

        // Check dependent services (optional)
        // Be careful: don't make health check call dependent services
        // as it can cause cascading health check failures

        HealthStatus status = new HealthStatus(
            healthy ? \"UP\" : \"DOWN\",
            details
        );

        return ResponseEntity
            .status(healthy ? HttpStatus.OK : HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE)
            .body(status);
    }
}
```

**Metadata Best Practices**:
- `version`: Application version for canary deployments
- `zone`: Availability zone for zone-aware routing
- `environment`: dev/test/staging/production for environment segmentation
- `capabilities`: Feature flags or capabilities (e.g., `supportsNewAPI=true`)
- `weight`: Traffic weight for weighted routing (e.g., `weight=100`)
